      "causes": ["hyp.dns-resolution"],
      "rationale": "A long case with a customer who guesses at first. All sites affected is a guess, a policy change turns out to have been made in a test tenant, a social-media claim of an outage is unverified, and Zabrze seems fine is hearsay. The engineer sends two policy detours (an exclusion test, a session revocation) although no failure record exists, which costs several hours, and only then asks for the site pattern, which shows that two sites share a resolver. The per-server comparison finds the resolver, the proxy nodes are consistent, the workaround goes site by site and two laptops with a typed-in server bring the problem back. The permanent fix and the before and after counts close the case.",
